WEBVTT

NOTE Paragraph boundaries measured from synthesis; timing within paragraphs is approximate.

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.964
Incident response
determines what happened,

00:00:02.964 --> 00:00:06.344
which systems are affected,
and what actions are justified.

00:00:06.344 --> 00:00:10.241
Digital forensics contributes
disciplined acquisition, preservation,

00:00:10.241 --> 00:00:14.423
and interpretation of artifacts.
Investigators work with identity events,

00:00:14.423 --> 00:00:18.033
process records, files, network
activity, and application logs.

00:00:18.033 --> 00:00:22.044
Models can extract and organize
details from approved evidence copies,

00:00:22.044 --> 00:00:25.940
but generating a narrative does
not replace collecting the evidence.

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:28.907
Timeline reconstruction
illustrates the distinction.

00:00:28.907 --> 00:00:31.418
A sign-in event,
an endpoint process record,

00:00:31.418 --> 00:00:34.842
and a network connection may
share a user or host reference.

00:00:34.842 --> 00:00:39.237
AI can place them in a proposed sequence
and identify gaps. Check time zones,

00:00:39.237 --> 00:00:43.345
clock differences, event identifiers,
and the meaning of each timestamp.

00:00:43.345 --> 00:00:47.454
Preserve original values when normalizing
time. A file modification time

00:00:47.454 --> 00:00:51.620
alone does not establish who changed
the file or which process caused it.

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:55.553
Correlating endpoint and network
records can suggest investigative leads,

00:00:55.553 --> 00:00:59.270
such as whether a process and connection
belong to the same activity.

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:03.202
Confirm the linkage using the available
identifiers and source artifacts.

00:01:03.202 --> 00:01:07.135
Missing logs may reflect retention
or collection gaps rather than absence

00:01:07.135 --> 00:01:11.390
of activity. Record both observed facts
and competing explanations; a plausible

00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:15.700
chain of events remains a hypothesis until
the supporting links are established.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:19.516
Preserve provenance by retaining
source references, acquisition context,

00:01:19.516 --> 00:01:23.331
and integrity information under the
investigation's evidence procedures.

00:01:23.331 --> 00:01:26.352
An AI-produced summary should
point back to those records

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:29.426
and distinguish confirmed scope
from unresolved questions.

00:01:29.426 --> 00:01:33.507
Containment authority remains separate
from suggesting an investigative lead.

00:01:33.507 --> 00:01:37.535
Incident response, forensic artifact
interpretation, and building a forensic

00:01:37.535 --> 00:01:41.562
toolkit each offer useful follow-up
study, because the quality of assistance

00:01:41.562 --> 00:01:45.060
depends on understanding what
the evidence can actually establish.
